WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.010
I Love You, Miss Noa

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.810
They aren't coming.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.360
They were supposed to be here already!

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.900
Are you sure you got
your facts straight?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.280
I'm positive!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.490
I overheard Goto on the phone.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.870
Kana Matsumoto will
join our team for a whole week!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.250
Who's Kana Matsumoto?

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.960
What?! You don't know her?

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.340
She's only the most popular
singer in all of Japan!

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.800
Izumi's more interested in
Alphonse than in idol singers.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.600
So, why is such a big star
joining our team, anyway?

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.770
She's going to learn
to pilot an Ingram.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.520
Next week, HQ is having a
Labor safety parade in Aoyama.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.730
Kana's going to lead
the entire parade in an Ingram.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:02.070
If this works, it'll do wonders
for Division 2's reputation!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.200
We'll get half-decent bonuses!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.080
Then we won't have to scavenge
around like rats any more!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.830
You'd better be right about this!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.210
I think they're here!

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.380
At attention everyone!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.560
Good, you're all here.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.320
I guess you've heard that we're
training a new member this week.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.330
This is Honorary Officer
Kana Matsumoto.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.080
Oh, yeah, guys! She's here!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:07.510
L-O-V-E! We love Kana!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.020
On behalf of Division 2,
allow me to welcome you.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.060
Thanks!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:20.900
Isao Ota,
serial number 0001, age 24!

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.280
Happy to be
at your service, anytime!

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.280
Thank you, Ota.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.490
Here's your mission:

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.330
You will teach Officer Matsumoto
how to pilot an Ingram.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.290
Officer Izumi, I appoint you
as her teacher.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.620
Who, me?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.170
I'll trade places with you!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.420
You're too reckless!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.590
What did you say?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:44.680
Come on, let's all get along,
and follow Izumi's lead in the training.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.090
That's all. Dismissed.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.970
I'm looking forward
to working with you.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.190
Move that carrier!

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.900
You lazy bums
can skip dinner tonight!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.620
I'm sure you've read the manual,
but there's the primary power.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.960
The pedals over there operate the legs.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.540
These levers control
the hands and arms.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.300
Uh, Asuma...

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.710
Relax! You'll be fine.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.760
Wait!

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:33.600
This is dangerous. What if
something happens to Alphonse?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.310
Come on, it's
just an initiation.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:41.020
The halls will ring with the victorious
voices of Division 2!

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.520
So shut up and help.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.280
It worked, Asuma.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.780
I turned on auto-pilot
during the deck-up.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.740
But wait, that's cheating.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.120
Naturally.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.700
A beginner needs to
gain confidence.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.120
If she's nervous, there's no way
she can learn this in a week.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.170
Was it this one? Maybe this.
Wait, how about this?

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.880
No. This? No.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.300
This?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.510
Please, God, let it be this one!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.850
All right! I'm ready!

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:12.510
Roger.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:16.560
Just relax, and move the Ingram
into the carrier.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.100
I know you can do it.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.270
Famous last words.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.230
Commence operation!

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.400
Here I go! Whee!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.070
You're the greatest, Kana!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.530
Okay. Now here...

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.630
Uh-oh!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.760
Oh, no!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.800
Alphonse!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.300
- Watch out!
- Let go!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.440
Alphonse!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.070
Alphonse!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:16.490
Kana?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.290
Oh, don't cry.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.250
You turned off your autopilot.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.420
See, take a look.
It's this switch here.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.590
I'm no good!

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.970
It happens all the time,
with beginners.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.800
Well, not really.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.890
I mean, don't worry!
You'll get better.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.390
Stop crying!

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.810
Your wounds will heal
on their own time.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:48.110
But you realize, it will take hard work
to fix these scratches on Alphonse!

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.660
That's enough for today.
Bring the crane.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.830
They're all just spoiling her!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.460
You can put up with it for a week.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.880
But she did manage to put
up her hands as she fell.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.470
She may actually
have some talent.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.550
Now even you're on her side!

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:18.810
I don't understand, why
does she have to use Alphonse?

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.770
Unit 3 is being used for parts
and isn't operational.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:26.770
And Ota has customized his Labor
too much for a beginner to handle.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.070
Excuse me, Izumi.
May I come in?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.910
I'm so sorry about today.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.450
I feel terrible about what happened.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.830
I'm just no good with machines.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.540
I can't even set the
clock on my VCR.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:51.000
But I really want to pilot a Labor!
Please don't give up on me!

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.590
Well, Izumi?
What's your answer?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:57.340
Oh, well.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.220
Training is hard, so
you'd better knuckle down.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.390
Yea!

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.520
Thank you!

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:11.150
I knew you were
nice the moment I met you!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.150
I just love you!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:25.040
Hold the gun in your right hand.
Aim carefully... and squeeze.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:30.790
Remember, the first shot
guarantees victory!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:33.380
Now, watch how a master does it.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:33.880
Okay!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.090
He's in a really good mood.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.600
Unreal!

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.520
Nothing to it, really!

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.400
Come on.
Get on with it.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:52.980
Okay.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.400
This one's for Izumi, with love.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.570
Here I go! Whee!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.070
What in the world was that all about?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.490
Just an innocent crush, like the way
girls get crushes in an all-girl school!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.330
I'm sure that's all!

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.020
I'd be surprised if she could skip
a bullet like that on purpose.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:29.980
Maybe.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.820
Are you okay with this?

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.530
Yeah, it's perfect timing.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.450
We needed to use more ammo
to justify our budget, anyway.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.240
That's not what I meant!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.660
If you're so busy
training this entertainer...

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.450
what happens if you're mobilized?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.080
Oh, is that what
you're worried about?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.290
Don't worry.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.170
Headquarters is really
gung ho on this parade.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.880
The media's going
to be there in force to see Kana.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.680
So our fearless leaders have
made this a top priority.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.850
We probably won't be
called out for a while, Shinobu.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.430
What if something big comes up?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.150
Then they probably
won't call MY division, right?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.620
Hello. Ryu here.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.910
Is the objective in sight?

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.580
It sure is.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.000
We just smuggled some missiles.
Now you want to kidnap a girl?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.340
I don't get it, boss.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.300
We're going after something big.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.050
This girl is just the first step
towards that goal.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.720
Don't disappoint me.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.560
Work it, girl!
Move those muscles!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.770
Izumi, haven't we had enough of this?

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.070
No chance!

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.610
A pilot's top requirement
in piloting a Labor is endurance!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:04.490
I'll get through with
wisdom and bravery.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.490
Can't we just quit for today?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:07.740
Weakling!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.950
If you don't work hard,
I won't lend you Alphonse!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.960
We're already halfway to
the Shanghai Restaurant.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.460
Come on, girl!

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.460
Work it!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.050
- With feeling!
- I'm feeling it!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.010
I can't hear you!

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:25.640
Work it!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.430
Working it!

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.220
Move it!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.140
Moving it!

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.850
Put some feeling into it!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:33.940
Shake it, girl!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.230
Keep it moving!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.150
I'm not hearing you!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.230
Come on!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.530
Work it! You okay back there?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:46.660
Kana?

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.760
Grau-Bear

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.560
Coming, coming!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.730
Hello? Special Vehicles,
Division 2.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.230
You've kidnapped Kana?!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.690
You'll need to hand over an
Ingram if you want her back.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.150
Who is this?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.610
You don't really expect me
to give you my name?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.860
So what's your answer,
yes or no?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.320
I'm back!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.290
Something the matter?

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.080
What'll it be?!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.370
Very funny,
ya sick prankster!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.630
Kana is right here!

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.710
Nice try, but I'm not a fool.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:43.670
Whatever!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.720
- I'm hanging up.
- Wait!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:50.600
You Japanese like to say
that "haste makes waste."

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.010
Is Kana Matsumoto
really there?

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.140
You're getting on my nerves.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.600
Hold on!
I'll check it out.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.480
Stop pulling pranks on the police!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:06.490
Does this have to do with me?

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:07.650
Hey, are you alone?

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.570
Weren't you with Noa?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:13.240
I lost sight of her.
Isn't she back yet?

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.960
It was dark and you
grabbed the wrong girl?!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.540
I couldn't tell them apart
from behind.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.550
Kidnapping a cop
won't do us any good.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.720
Losing the entertainer would
have embarrassed the police...

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.720
and they would have
traded an Ingram for her.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.760
But they won't trade now.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.800
I'm sorry.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.060
Oh, well.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.810
Maybe I can rely on the forgiving
nature of the Japanese.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.200
There's no choice.
We have to do it.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.160
Noa's life depends on it!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.790
You can't give them an Ingram!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.330
Izumi is a police officer!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:00.920
She should've committed suicide
as soon as she was captured!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:01.750
Zip it!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.040
It's all my fault!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:07.340
If only I hadn't lost sight of her!

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.470
Don't blame yourself, Kana!

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.800
Hello? This is Officer
Asuma Shinohara speaking.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.810
Ah... Officer Shinohara.
I'm willing to discuss...

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.730
You'll get your Ingram!
Don't you dare hurt Noa!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.560
I mean, Officer Izumi.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:24.190
You'll go for it?

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.020
I don't lie.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.440
Yes... midnight.
The burger shop on the landfill.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.650
Got it.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.450
I'll come alone with the Ingram.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.240
Let's ask HQ.
Better call for backup.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.580
And what's HQ going to
opt to protect?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.080
An unlucky policewoman
or a top-of-the-line Ingram?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.120
The Ingram, of course.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.920
So, we'll have to do this on our own.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.510
We can't even tell the captain.
Remember, Noa has to come first!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:51.470
I understand.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.390
We won't give
them Izumi OR the Ingram!

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.010
Kana, you wait here.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.600
Wait...

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.730
Izumi...

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.160
Don't be so pushy!

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.450
Hello.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.620
Kidnapping me isn't going
to get you an Ingram!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:30.090
You're a gutsy young lady,
but I'm afraid you're wrong.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.170
I am?

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.470
Excuse me. Clam up!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.390
Some errors were made,
but I still managed to close the deal.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:41.430
I'll strip it for parts and
sell it to a foreign army.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:45.810
The autostabilizer
alone will make me rich!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:46.860
Merchant of Death!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:50.530
I'd get a better price
if I threw in the pilot!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.900
Be quiet, and you won't get hurt.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.150
Welcome! The menu's right above.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:27.900
Uh, well...

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.820
Keep quiet.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:33.780
You bastard!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.740
We have a special on hamburgers.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.950
Did you bring the goods?

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.370
How about a nice,
hot cup of coffee?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.420
The woman goes
free once we
leave Japan.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.710
Hand over the system disk.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.840
Would you like fries with that?

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.680
I'll ask you to pay in advance.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.560
Thank you.
Come again!

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.770
Damn!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:16.990
You'll get yours!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.740
- Don't let him spot us!
- I won't.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.090
Shinohara here.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.970
Subject is heading for Urayasu.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.260
Roger.
Wait until I get there.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.080
Over there.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.060
Halt! Where's Noa?

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:31.270
Ouch! Let me go!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.560
If anything happens to me,
I can't guarantee her safety!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.230
And if you've done
anything to Noa...

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:38.530
I'll kill you.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.940
That's enough.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:41.490
Noa!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.450
Asuma, I'm sorry!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.160
Release Ryu.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.160
What's taking Ota?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.580
What?

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.840
Izumi, I'll avenge your death!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.460
I'm not dead yet!

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.590
I'll be your pallbearer!

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:10.680
Let me go!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:15.310
Your powerful Ingram
has been rendered helpless!

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:19.480
Ryu, get on board our Ingram
and eliminate these pests!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.570
Okay, boss!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:21.650
Don't!

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.320
Keep your grubby
hands off my Alphonse!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.210
Hey my Alphonse would never do that!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.590
Izumi, I did it!

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.010
Kana!

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.890
What's going on?

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:54.270
Asuma! Kanuka!

00:20:55.140 --> 00:21:00.650
Back off, minions of evil!
Don't you see this crest?

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.440
You've fallen into our trap!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.410
Help me, boss!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.660
You're not going anywhere!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.630
Help me!

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.750
Are you all right, Kana?

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:23.090
Halt!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.840
Never underestimate
the Japanese police!

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.390
Oh, boy, now the captain's going
to find out for sure.

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.270
You mean,
he doesn't know about this yet?

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.730
How stupid do you think we are?

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:39.270
I'm sorry.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.320
I'm just glad you're safe.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.190
Everything will be fine... probably.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:51.160
That's not playing fair,
hiding a pilot in the Ingram cockpit!

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.120
All's fair in the name of justice!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:10.010
Izumi, I've decided to set you free.

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:14.390
It's obvious that Asuma is
nuts about you.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.520
No! It isn't like that at all!

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:19.560
Yeah, what he says!

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.190
Will you shut up?

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.780
Hurry up, before the captain sees us.

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.740
What are you all up to?

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:32.160
You're sure early.
I've got hot coffee on.

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:37.910
And I picked up fries, too!
Any takers?

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:45.800
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:49.510
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:55.770
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.270
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:08.190
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:12.780
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.450
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.290
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.460
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:30.970
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:36.220
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:38.770
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:41.980
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:46.070
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:52.240
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:58.290
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:04.920
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:09.840
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:09.840
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:19.430
Plans are now underway to build a vast
underground city called Tokyo Geo-city.

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:24.850
It all started with one little hole
in the artificial underground highway.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:28.400
Into that hole we tracked some deadly
terrorists, and we encountered...

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:29.610
a giant, black shadow.

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:32.780
Ingram #2 is trapped!
You'll have to go on without me.

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:35.160
Next episode:
"The Shadow of Geo-Front."

00:24:35.160 --> 00:24:36.660
Target locked on!

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:40.870
Next episode

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:40.870
The Shadow of Geo-Front
